# This is the ignore file Vercel actually reads — Root Directory is the repo
# root, not public/, so a .vercelignore sitting inside public/ (there is one,
# kept as a tested manifest of the deploy's public surface) is never
# consulted. outputDirectory already scopes what's SERVED to public/ alone;
# this file only trims what gets uploaded, and above all keeps secrets that
# happen to sit at the repo root off Vercel's servers entirely.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
sovereign.config.json
sovereign.config.*.json
*.log
data
models
node_modules
.git
